		{
			"id": "eLTWnpWvJYXgNLmW8",
			"description": "Flak Vest",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nCovers torso only. Worn over fatigues; does not interfere with Stealth the way rigid plate does.\n\nLore: The standard-issue ballistic vest of the Astra Militarum: overlapping plasteel or ceramic plates sewn into a fabric carrier. Depicted throughout Guard-focused Black Library fiction (e.g. the Gaunt's Ghosts and Ciaphas Cain series) as adequate against shrapnel and stubber fire but routinely shrugged past by las-weapons at range and always by bolt weapons.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 30, the framework's flak anchor (raised from 12 at the user's direction to make Guard armour tougher). Exact odds per hit: lasgun 7d(2) 98%, laspistol 4d(2) 34%, autogun 7d 9%, autopistol 0%. Flak now stops most solid-slug fire, matching the original lore line that flak stops stub rounds, while las still gets through. No coverage elsewhere: a vest stops at the shoulders and waist. Cost and weight are estimates scaled below mesh and well below carapace.",
