		{
			"id": "eWlmu5mW39ZFRryfO",
			"description": "Flak Coat, Death Korps Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nAnkle-length greatcoat with a quilted flak liner; often worn with a Death Korps gas-hood (see Respirator, Imperial Field Gear) rather than a separate helmet.\n\nLore: The Death Korps of Krieg's iconic heavy greatcoat is depicted in Forge World's Imperial Armour background and in Black Library's Krieg-focused fiction as a full-length, gas-sealed coat rather than a vest, reflecting the regiment's siege-warfare and toxic-battlefield doctrine.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 30 (flak anchor); the coat's extra length buys leg coverage, not thicker plate. Arms and legs 23, matching the Flak Jacket.",
