		{
			"id": "eoYuDRvD6t1D0aY-v",
			"description": "Flak Armour, Full Suit (Cadian Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nVest, pauldrons and leggings worn as a matched set; pairs with the Flak Helmet below for full coverage. The Cadian pattern (moulded breastplate over a grey bodyglove) is the Munitorum's most widely issued flak set and the visual template most Guard regiments are equipped from.\n\nLore: Cadian Shock Troops are the Munitorum's default visual and doctrinal template for Guard infantry across Codex Astra Militarum background and Black Library fiction (Cadian-focused novels). Other regiments field their own cut of the same flak principle: Mordian dress-pattern jackets, Vostroyan quilted coats, Tallarn wraps, Catachan shirtless carapace-less troopers who often forgo the torso plate altogether for heat and mobility.\n\nDesign: Same profile as the Flak Coat: torso 30 (flak anchor), arms and legs 23. The full suit buys a matched, fitted kit rather than a higher number; regimental variation is flavour, not stats.",
