		{
			"id": "ep1GWZYb675FeSSPM",
			"description": "Flak Helmet, Cadian Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nOpen-faced; no eye or face protection. Some patterns (Mordian, Death Korps) add a neck flap worth a point or two of DR at the GM's discretion.\n\nLore: The classic Guard helmet: a domed plasteel/ceramite shell with a chinstrap and no visor, seen across nearly every piece of Astra Militarum art and background from the Uplifting Primer excerpts onward.\n\nDesign: Skull DR 25, the framework's flak helmet anchor. Open face is a lore call: Guard helmets are consistently drawn without a visor.",
