		{
			"id": "eGlzlZ8NNeUfLTYKk",
			"description": "Mesh Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 6: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 6 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour: treat blunt/crushing damage that fails to penetrate as normal per the flexible-armour rule (blunt trauma still applies even when DR stops the attack).\n\nLore: Fine metal-weave armour worn under fashionable clothing by hive nobility, Officio Assassinorum operatives, and Inquisitorial agents who need protection without looking armoured. Described across Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader-line background and hive-noble scenes in Black Library fiction (the Eisenhorn and Ravenor series) as concealable and comfortable but not rigid.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 36, the framework's mesh anchor, flexible (GURPS flexible-armour rules: stops penetration, not blunt trauma; see notes). Arms and legs 29, neck 21, keeping the earlier limb ratios. Hands, feet and head uncovered: a bodysuit worn under clothes.",
