		{
			"id": "eRn4aEzO0wGIbmp9v",
			"description": "Carapace Armour, Guard Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nRigid plate over a padded underlayer; imposes the usual GURPS bulky-armour DX/Stealth penalties for rigid heavy armour.\n\nLore: Moulded plasteel plate issued to elite Guard formations (storm troopers historically, tank crew, and veteran squads) and worn as a full body shell with integral or paired helmet. Only War and Dark Heresy background consistently place carapace a clear step above flak and a clear step below power armour, which the anchor table encodes directly.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 70, the framework's carapace anchor (raised from 45 at the user's direction). Exact odds per hit: lasgun 7d(2) 0.6%, long-las 8d(2) 6%, hellgun 8d(3) 82%, bolter 79%. Carapace is close to immune to standard las fire; hellguns and bolters are what beat it. Arms, legs and neck 52, skull 64, face and feet 36, eye 20 (lowered for the Weak Points and eye-lens rule; see framework.md), keeping the earlier location ratios; hands uncovered (gauntlets are separate).",
