		{
			"id": "eopjW8uypwAd9qGWn",
			"description": "Carapace Armour, Tempestus Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nVoid-sealed; can be worn in vacuum or toxic atmosphere for short periods without a separate rebreather. Rigid heavy armour DX/Stealth penalties apply.\n\nLore: The maroon-and-grey carapace of the Tempestus Scions (and their forerunners, Storm Troopers) is depicted across Codex Astra Militarum and Only War background and in Black Library fiction (widely depicted; no single source) as better-fitted and more complete than line-Guard carapace, closing the gaps at the hands, feet and joints that standard-issue kit leaves open, and rated for drop-pod and high-altitude insertion.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 70 (carapace anchor). Elite carapace isn't a thicker category; its edge is coverage: hands and feet protected, and limbs and neck (64) sit closer to torso than the Guard pattern's, for tighter, better-forged fit. Skull 70, face and feet 42, hands 36, eye 20.",
