		{
			"id": "e0AfCS25TMCguhUyF",
			"description": "Carapace Armour, Arbites Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFull-face armoured mask standard; the enclosed helm and shoulder guards read as unmistakably Arbites on sight, which the GM may use for Intimidation or Fast-Talk reaction penalties against criminal or hive-ganger NPCs. Rigid heavy armour DX/Stealth penalties apply.\n\nLore: Adeptus Arbites Judges wear a distinct black or grey carapace pattern built for riot control and room-clearing rather than open-field war: an enclosed, masked helm (unlike the Guard's open one), shoulder guards, and a design meant to intimidate a hab-block as much as protect the wearer. Depicted in Black Library's Warhammer Crime line and in Codex and Necromunda background (widely depicted; no single source).\n\nDesign: Torso DR 70 (carapace anchor). Like the Tempestus pattern it adds full head enclosure and hand/foot coverage for close-quarters hab clearance: limbs 56, neck 64, skull 70, face 52, feet 42, hands 36, eye 20 (lowered for the Weak Points and eye-lens rule; see framework.md).",
