		{
			"id": "ePCo8cL0v7BnHlAD0",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark IV (Maximus Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nInterlocking plate sections reduce the usual bulky-armour penalty by 1 relative to other Marks at the GM's discretion (still requires the black carapace interface).\n\nLore: Mark IV \"Maximus Armour\" introduced overlapping, interlocking plates and improved articulation partway through the Horus Heresy, trading a little of Mark III's raw frontal thickness for a suit Legion armourers could produce faster and Astartes could fight in more freely — the pattern most associated with the war's mid-to-late battles in Black Library's Horus Heresy series.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 95, 5 below the Mark VII baseline and 3 above the Mark II: the fiction frames Mark IV as a mobility improvement over Mark III, not a protection one, so the DR number sits at the \"lighter\" end of the spread — the improvement is represented instead as a reduced bulk penalty called out in `notes`. Eye lenses fixed at 40 as with every other mark.",
