		{
			"id": "eKCZGlz-VH4P7kfDK",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark V (Heresy Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nA hybrid/composite suit: individual pieces may visibly mismatch (Mark II vambraces on a Mark IV chestpiece, etc.) with no mechanical effect beyond what's already priced in below. Requires the black carapace interface.\n\nLore: Mark V \"Heresy Armour\" is the composite pattern that emerged as Legion forges struggled to keep pace with attrition during the war's later years: earlier-mark components refitted and combined with whatever a forge or salvage crew had on hand. Horus Heresy-era Black Library fiction repeatedly shows Astartes wearing visibly patchwork plate by this stage of the war.\n\nDesign: Torso DR set just below the general -5-from-baseline cluster (93) to reflect inconsistent manufacture and scavenged parts — the framework's Mark spread is ±10–15, and a composite suit built from mismatched salvage is reasoned to sit at the lower edge of that range rather than the middle. Eye lenses fixed at 40 as with every mark.",
