		{
			"id": "eOtsVy18LGc4CwGhD",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark VI (Corvus Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nReduced bulk penalty (as Mark IV) reflecting the pattern's emphasis on speed. Requires the black carapace interface.\n\nLore: Mark VI \"Corvus Armour\" — the famous \"beaky\" helm pattern — is depicted across Horus Heresy background and later flashback fiction as deliberately lighter and faster than its predecessors, developed by the Raven Guard's Corvus Corax and adopted widely for its mobility, at a real cost in raw protection compared to heavier Heresy-era plate.\n\nDesign: Torso DR set at the bottom of the framework's ±10–15 spread (88, -12), the lightest of the Heresy-era marks modelled here, directly reflecting the \"lighter\" framing consistently attached to this pattern in the lore. Eye lenses fixed at 40 as with every mark; the reduced-bulk note mirrors Mark IV's for the same reason (both patterns are explicitly about trading plate for speed).",
