		{
			"id": "EZVVq-h5K5rbtDjIl",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark VII (Aquila Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nThis is the framework's baseline pattern; treat its numbers as the reference point every other Mark is compared against. Requires the black carapace interface: an Astartes without one (very rare; the implant is standard by the time a Scout is elevated) fights at -4 DX and half Basic Move in this suit and cannot use its auto-senses or weapon interlocks. A non-Astartes human forced into Mark VII plate (e.g. by an Inquisitor's agent testing a relic suit) suffers the same penalties and additionally cannot engage the suit's fine motor control at all for tasks finer than walking and gross gestures — the black carapace is what translates a wearer's nervous system directly into the suit's servo response, and nothing else substitutes for it.\n\nLore: Mark VII \"Aquila Armour\" is the standardised post-Heresy pattern issued across the newly re-formed Chapters and remains, per current Codex Space Marines background and countless 41st-millennium Black Library novels, the most commonly depicted Astartes plate to this day.\n\nDesign: Torso DR and eye-lens DR are both taken directly from the fixed anchor (\"Astartes power armour (Mk VII baseline) | 100 ... Eye lenses DR 40\", framework.md); every other Mark in this file is derived relative to this entry. Limb/head DR are torso minus 12 for arms and legs, minus 25 for face and feet, and minus 37 for neck and hands; the Mark II to Mark VI patterns keep these offsets. The Mark VII's own servo bonus (lifting +9, striking +5) is the reference value the other marks scale from. GCS adds a container's children to its own weight and cost, so the shell entry is the plate itself (150 lb, $40,000); with its subsystems (90 lb, $30,000) the assembled suit is 240 lb and $70,000. The servo bonus lives on the Servo-Motor Actuators child only, so it is counted once.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
