		{
			"id": "eg-griLH1lcViKyvu",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark X (Tacticus Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nRequires the black carapace interface; Primaris Space Marines receive an enhanced black carapace as part of their creation, per current background, but the interface requirement and its penalties for an unaugmented wearer are unchanged.\n\nLore: Mark X \"Tacticus Armour\" is the standard-issue plate of the Primaris Space Marines introduced in current-edition Codex Space Marines background and the Dark Imperium/Guilliman-era Black Library novels: a modern synthesis of earlier design principles built for a taller, more heavily muscled Primaris physiology.\n\nDesign: Torso DR set 8 above the Mark VII baseline (108), reflecting current background's framing of Tacticus plate as an incremental, modern refinement rather than a radical departure — still within the framework's ±10–15 spread. Slightly higher servo ST than Mark VII reflects the larger Primaris frame the suit is built around, though this project keeps Primaris ST as a trait-file matter, not an armour one; the bonus here is the suit's own contribution only.",
