		{
			"id": "ei7bVxs1_4yOQ0guZ",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark X (Phobos Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nRequires the black carapace interface. Lighter and quieter than baseline Tacticus plate; the reduced bulk lessens (but does not remove) the usual rigid heavy armour Stealth penalty, represented as the Stealth bonus above.\n\nLore: Mark X \"Phobos Armour\" equips Primaris infiltrators, reivers and incursors: current Codex Space Marines background describes it as deliberately stripped down for stealth insertion and reconnaissance, sacrificing plate thickness for silence, sensor equipment and low signature.\n\nDesign: Torso DR set at the bottom of the framework's spread (88), matching Mark VI's lightweight reasoning for the same trade-off (speed and stealth over raw protection). Eye-lens DR is 36, nudged from the shared 40 (90%) since the pattern's sensor visor is optimised for passive detection rather than ballistic resistance, a deliberate, called-out departure from the \"same component reused\" assumption used elsewhere, justified by Phobos gear's explicit stealth-first design brief. The Stealth skill bonus has no anchor and is a reasoned estimate for \"lighter and quieter than the baseline suit.\"",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
