		{
			"id": "elgL_PoMLnbBnWTfu",
			"description": "Power Armour, Mark X (Gravis Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nHeavier and slower than standard plate; the wearer suffers an extra -1 Basic Move from bulk (already applied above) on top of the usual rigid heavy armour penalties. Requires the black carapace interface.\n\nLore: Mark X \"Gravis Armour\" is described in current Codex Space Marines background as heavy-assault plate for Primaris Aggressors, Eradicators, and similar close-support roles: thicker than any other power-armour pattern short of Terminator plate, explicitly a step between standard power armour and Tactical Dreadnought armour.\n\nDesign: Torso DR is its own fixed anchor (130, framework.md: \"Between power armour and Terminator plate\"), deliberately breaking the ±10–15 spread that governs every other power-armour Mark in this file, because the lore explicitly places Gravis between the Mark VII baseline (100) and the Tactical Dreadnought anchor (200): 130 sits roughly a third of the way up that gap, reflecting \"heavier than standard plate, well short of Terminator plate.\" Limbs sit lower than torso by 17 (arms and legs), 24 (face), 31 (feet), 35 (neck) and 47 (hands), with eye-lens DR 50, the midpoint of the Mark VII (40) and Terminator (60) lenses. Servo ST bonus is raised well above every other power-armour Mark for the same reason, and a small Basic Move penalty is added since the suit trades mobility for that extra plate.",
