		{
			"id": "eWFN13qARcUM3vd_g",
			"description": "Scout Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 6: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 6 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nUnpowered partial plate: chestpiece, backplate and a groin/thigh guard worn over fatigues, with no helmet, gauntlets or servo-motors. Does not require the black carapace interface, since most Chapters implant it later in a Scout's development (widely depicted; the exact order of implantation varies by Chapter).\n\nLore: Scout Marines — Astartes neophytes who have not yet completed the full gene-seed implantation and elevation to the battle-brotherhood — fight in simpler, partial plate over fatigues rather than full power armour, consistent with their depiction across Black Library's Scout-focused fiction (the Raven Guard and Space Wolves Scout novels among others) and current Codex Space Marines background.\n\nDesign: Not full plate, so no power-armour anchor applies. Torso DR 77: the carapace anchor (70) plus a small premium for Astartes-grade materials. Coverage is deliberately partial (legs 36; no head, arm, hand or foot plate) for the half-armoured silhouette Scouts are drawn with. No servo-motor ST bonus: the suit is unpowered.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "8000",
			"base_weight": "40 lb",
