		{
			"id": "EPLUwRRIKljNDxmH9",
			"description": "Tactical Dreadnought Armour, Indomitus Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 3: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 3 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nEffective SM +1 while worn (bigger target, but also greater reach and a larger surface for called shots); on top of the usual rigid heavy armour penalties, treat DX-based fine work as at an extra -2 due to the suit's thick, servo-assisted gauntlets. Life support lets the wearer survive teleport-assault insertion and short vacuum/void operations. Requires the black carapace interface.\n\nLore: \"Terminator\" plate — modern Indomitus-pattern Tactical Dreadnought Armour — is the heaviest power armour a Space Marine can wear and fight in, reserved for a Chapter's most veteran warriors and for the most desperate close-quarters actions (teleport assaults into enemy strongholds, boarding actions). Current Codex Space Marines background and countless Black Library depictions describe it as effectively a one-Astartes tank: it shrugs off small-arms and bolter fire and is brought down only by heavy weapons, power fists, or comparable threats.\n\nDesign: Torso DR taken directly from the fixed anchor (\"Tactical Dreadnought (Terminator) | 200, Ignores bolters. Plasma, lascannon, power fist and thunder hammer still kill.\", framework.md). Limbs sit lower than torso by 25 (arms and legs), 50 (face and feet), 62 (neck) and 75 (hands); eye lenses 60. SM +1 is taken directly from framework.md's \"a Terminator can be SM +1\" note; the Basic Move penalty and extra DX note represent the suit's bulk in mechanical terms the anchor doesn't itself specify. GCS adds a container's children to its own weight and cost, so the shell carries only the plate (300 lb, $120,000); with the children (180 lb, $90,000) the assembled suit is 480 lb and $210,000. The servo bonus (lifting +20, striking +10) lives on the Servo-Motor Actuators child only, so it is counted once.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
