			"children": [
				{
					"id": "eYIXNxQCm-FzC8Iyd",
					"description": "Auto-senses Suite (Terminator Pattern)",
					"local_notes": "Enhanced sensor package feeding a wider helm display; functionally similar to the Mark VII suite but built into a much larger helm.\n\nLore: Terminator squads are consistently shown operating with excellent situational awareness despite the suit's bulk.\n\nDesign: Same bonus as the Mark VII Auto-senses Suite; no lore basis for a numeric difference, only a cosmetic one (bigger helm, same sensor doctrine).",
					"base_value": "10000",
					"base_weight": "6 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Observation"
							},
							"amount": 2
						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "euUWaPZIWJF6LQHmS",
					"description": "Vox-Link (Integrated)",
					"local_notes": "Long-range, high-power vox suited to boarding actions and teleport strikes where a squad may be cut off from wider support.\n\nLore: Teleport assault doctrine (Codex background, Black Library boarding-action fiction) depends on reliable vox once a squad is deep inside enemy territory.\n\nDesign: Flavour/utility subsystem; no DR or attribute effect.",
					"base_value": "3000",
					"base_weight": "3 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eaj-fskv9Voja1aOj",
					"description": "Storm Bolter Mag-Lock Mount",
					"local_notes": "Combined weapon-mount and ammunition feed hardware for the suit's signature storm bolter/power fist loadout; the weapons themselves are not part of this file.\n\nLore: Terminators are almost always depicted armed with a storm bolter and power fist or matched pair of lightning claws, integrated into the suit's forearms.\n\nDesign: Flavour/mounting-hardware subsystem, priced separately from the weapons it carries.",
					"base_value": "5000",
					"base_weight": "10 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "e_z7q-_Zbf-6cFkii",
					"description": "Respirator & Full Void Seal",
					"local_notes": "Complete atmospheric independence, including extended vacuum survival for teleport strikes directly into voidborne hulks and enemy ships.\n\nLore: A staple of boarding-action fiction across the setting.\n\nDesign: Heavier/more thorough version of the Mark VII equivalent, priced up accordingly; no separate anchor.",
					"base_value": "6000",
					"base_weight": "10 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "e1W7-onldke-oHa1n",
					"description": "Recyclers (Extended)",
					"local_notes": "Extended-endurance air and water reclamation for long teleport-strike or void-war deployments.\n\nLore: Consistent with Astartes endurance background.\n\nDesign: Flavour subsystem, no mechanical bonus.",
					"base_value": "4000",
					"base_weight": "8 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "ebGvyygHNDpn9Oxio",
					"description": "Servo-Motor Actuators (Terminator Pattern)",
					"local_notes": "The largest and most powerful servo package in this file; the bulk of the suit's weight and cost.\n\nLore: Terminators are depicted punching through bulkheads and grappling with things no unarmoured human could touch, consistent with a major step up in raw powered strength over standard plate.\n\nDesign: ST bonus set well above every standard power-armour Mark, reflecting both the heavier plate the motors need to move and the suit's role fighting things far tougher than the standard's baseline.",
					"base_value": "62000",
					"base_weight": "143 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "lifting_st",
							"amount": 20
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "striking_st",
							"amount": 10
						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "efvo63jiKO-zUkWt1",
			"description": "Tactical Dreadnought Armour, Tartaros Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 3: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 3 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nEffective SM +1 while worn. Lighter and faster than Cataphractii plate: Basic Move -1 like Indomitus, but the gauntlets are less clumsy, so treat DX-based fine work as an extra -1 rather than -2. Requires the black carapace interface.\n\nLore: Tartaros is the Horus Heresy-era Terminator pattern built for boarding actions and fast assault: lighter and more mobile than the older Cataphractii plate, with a lower profile and a more integrated weapon mount, per Forge World's Horus Heresy background and Black Library's Horus Heresy series. It sits between the Mark VII power armour and the later Indomitus plate in protection.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 190, 10 under the Tactical Dreadnought anchor (200) and 30 under Cataphractii (220): the lore places it as the lightest of the Terminator patterns. Limbs sit lower than torso by 25 (arms and legs), 50 (face and feet), 62 (neck) and 75 (hands), the Indomitus offsets; eye lenses 60 and Weak Points 3 as every Terminator plate. Servo bonus (lifting +18, striking +9) sits between the Mark VII's (9/5) and the Indomitus's (20/10). Weight 250 lb (Mark VII 150, Indomitus 300) and cost $100,000 ($120,000 for Indomitus) follow the same interpolation. SM +1 and Basic Move -1 as Indomitus. Built as a single item with the servo bonus on the parent and no children, like Cataphractii, so nothing is counted twice.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
