		{
			"id": "eeD1JjuOkX6BoU_rz",
			"description": "Tactical Dreadnought Armour, Cataphractii Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 3: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 3 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nEffective SM +1 while worn, as Indomitus pattern, but heavier still: an extra -1 Basic Move (net -2 total) and treat DX-based fine work at an extra -2, as Indomitus. Requires the black carapace interface.\n\nLore: Cataphractii is the older, Horus Heresy-era Terminator pattern: even more heavily armoured and correspondingly slower than the later Indomitus pattern that superseded it, per Forge World's Horus Heresy background and Black Library's Horus Heresy series, where Cataphractii- armoured Terminators are repeatedly described as nigh-unstoppable but ponderous.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 220, 20 above the Tactical Dreadnought anchor (200), justified by the lore's explicit framing of Cataphractii as heavier than modern Terminator plate; the anchor value is treated as the Indomitus/modern baseline. Limbs sit lower than torso by 32 (arms and legs), 57 (face and feet), 69 (neck) and 82 (hands); eye lenses 60, equal to Indomitus. Weak Points 3 as every Terminator plate. An extra point of Basic Move penalty (net -2) represents the pattern's greater ponderousness relative to Indomitus plate.",
